From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: elkir0 <elkir0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] ARM: dts: gts28ltexx: the G3D block from aclk_g3d_400,
 and SYSREG_G3D

The GPU's clock comes from CMU_TOP's aclk_g3d_400 at 800/3 MHz instead
of the G3D PLL the bootloader left at 266 MHz, the rate within 0.25 %.
CMU_G3D's own registers are clocked from the same mux: behind the PLL,
gating the GPU clock stopped the PLL (pll_35xx has a disable op), and
CMU_G3D's runtime suspend, which reads its registers next, hung the bus
at panfrost's first runtime suspend (2026-11-04).  CMU_G3D holds
aclk_g3d_400 while it is resumed.

SYSREG_G3D gets a syscon node, for panfrost to set the G3D block's NoC
timeout again after each power-on of pd_g3d, as the vendor kernel did.
Nothing else touches it, and only with the domain on.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../samsung/exynos5433-gts28ltexx-gpu.dtsi    | 31 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 31 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/samsung/exynos5433-gts28ltexx-gpu.dtsi b/arch/arm/boot/dts/samsung/exynos5433-gts28ltexx-gpu.dtsi
index 9bbbbebab..96849e68f 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/samsung/exynos5433-gts28ltexx-gpu.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/samsung/exynos5433-gts28ltexx-gpu.dtsi
@@ -15,6 +15,17 @@
  * here.
  */
 
+&soc {
+	/*
+	 * SYSREG_G3D (kernel_universal5433 mach/map.h:327), inside pd_g3d:
+	 * only panfrost's power-on quirk touches it, with the domain on.
+	 */
+	sysreg_g3d: syscon@14a90000 {
+		compatible = "samsung,exynos5433-sysreg", "syscon";
+		reg = <0x14a90000 0x1000>;
+	};
+};
+
 &gpu {
 	/*
 	 * GPU rail: BUCK6, "vdd_g3d" in the stock tree (live_fdt.dts:2399-2407)
@@ -30,6 +41,26 @@ &gpu {
 	mali-supply = <&buck6_reg>;
 	status = "okay";
 
+	/*
+	 * The G3D block runs from CMU_TOP's aclk_g3d_400 at 800/3 MHz, not
+	 * from the G3D PLL the bootloader left at 266 MHz.  CMU_G3D's own
+	 * registers are clocked from that same mux: with the PLL behind it,
+	 * gating the GPU clock stopped the PLL (pll_35xx has a disable op)
+	 * and CMU_G3D's runtime suspend, which reads its registers next,
+	 * hung the bus at panfrost's first runtime suspend (2026-11-04).
+	 * From aclk_g3d_400, which CMU_G3D holds while it is resumed
+	 * (clk-exynos-arm64.c exynos_arm64_cmu_resume()), the registers keep
+	 * a clock until the unit has switched itself to OSCCLK and released
+	 * it.  The rate stays the same within 0.25 %.
+	 */
+	assigned-clocks = <&cmu_g3d CLK_MOUT_ACLK_G3D_400>,
+			  <&cmu_top CLK_DIV_ACLK_G3D_400>;
+	assigned-clock-parents = <&cmu_top CLK_ACLK_G3D_400>, <0>;
+	assigned-clock-rates = <0>, <266666667>;
+
+	/* the NoC timeout that a power-off of pd_g3d clears (panfrost_gpu.c) */
+	samsung,sysreg = <&sysreg_g3d>;
+
 	/*
 	 * No OPP table, hence no devfreq: panfrost_devfreq_init() returns 0
 	 * when the device has no table (panfrost_devfreq.c:151-157) and the
-- 
